# animate exec prices a dot product and a matrix product as their
# multiply-adds (one multiply and K - 1 multiply-adds for each K-term
# dot), each fmul, times the f64 factor in f64; a transpose only moves
#
# a dot of dvec3: three f64 multiply-adds (97.125 under gt1030)
animate exec seed 1 nofile
```glsl
float h(vec3 a, vec3 b) { dvec3 A = dvec3(a), B = dvec3(b); return float(dot(A, B)); }
```
# dmat2 * dvec2: four
animate exec seed 1 nofile
```glsl
float h2(vec2 a, mat2 m) { dvec2 A = dvec2(a); dmat2 M = dmat2(m); return float((M * A).x); }
```
# mat3 * vec3 in f32: nine fmul, and a transpose costs nothing
animate exec seed 1 nofile
```glsl
vec3 h3(vec3 a, mat3 m) { return transpose(m) * a; }
```
